1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,340
Weather-or-Not.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:03,020
The utility says it was the weather.

3
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:04,610
Weather-or-Not checks.

4
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:07,313
A solo entry from Singapore.

5
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:11,287
An analyst is handed a filing that credits colder weather.

6
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,787
Checking it means peers, degree days,

7
00:00:14,107 --> 00:00:16,767
and a comparative column that a later filing can restate:

8
00:00:17,227 --> 00:00:22,547
American Electric Power's own 10-Q reports 5,463.4 million;

9
00:00:23,147 --> 00:00:26,947
the next year's restates it as 5,463.0.

10
00:00:27,627 --> 00:00:31,837
Rule R1 keeps the quarter's own filing and records the conflict.

11
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,660
The analyst picks FirstEnergy, the first quarter of 2025,

12
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,070
and the claim: colder weather.

13
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:47,007
Each chunk streams as the local Nemotron model plans it.

14
00:00:47,387 --> 00:00:49,367
The planner's text is shown as a plan,

15
00:00:49,607 --> 00:00:52,997
never as a fact; only tool rows carry numbers.

16
00:00:54,315 --> 00:00:56,695
Degree days are computed in Lightning SQL,

17
00:00:57,195 --> 00:00:58,455
about 20 seconds a quarter;

18
00:00:58,895 --> 00:01:01,085
the whole question takes about two minutes.

19
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,960
Revenue rose 14.5% like for like.

20
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:15,120
Weather is consistent with 8.2 points of that,

21
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:21,240
range 1.6 to 14.0; industry 2.9; the remainder 3.5.

22
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:24,680
Supported, with high confidence: 39 peers,

23
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:28,830
coverage 1.00, and the data-quality gate passed.

24
00:01:33,967 --> 00:01:35,167
Every figure is a button.

25
00:01:35,687 --> 00:01:38,147
The citation is the Lightning SQL itself:

26
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:40,567
the statement, its hash, the rows,

27
00:01:40,787 --> 00:01:42,567
the Zetaris object, the endpoint,

28
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:45,017
the licence and the retrieval time.

29
00:01:48,133 --> 00:01:51,653
In Zetaris Lightning, SEC EDGAR is a set of REST tables

30
00:01:51,673 --> 00:01:55,233
and NOAA GHCN-Daily a set of parquet tables;

31
00:01:55,753 --> 00:01:58,653
the weather_or_not_usl semantic layer joins

32
00:01:58,673 --> 00:02:01,243
them with keys and a data-quality rule.

33
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,980
The layer has five tables with primary and

34
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,640
foreign keys and nine data-quality rules;

35
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:11,490
the coverage_ok rule on weather_quarter gates every verdict.

36
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:14,473
Memory and why.

37
00:02:14,973 --> 00:02:17,253
The restatement is a conflict in H-MEM

38
00:02:17,273 --> 00:02:18,833
with both accession numbers;

39
00:02:19,293 --> 00:02:22,483
the why trace shows the fact's provenance and its trust ledger.

40
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:29,413
The analyst can override rule R1 with a reason.

41
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:32,873
The server signs a single-use high-risk contract,

42
00:02:33,073 --> 00:02:36,423
applies the override, and the ledger records who decided.

43
00:02:39,467 --> 00:02:41,767
The World Model keeps utilities, states,

44
00:02:42,147 --> 00:02:44,147
stations and filings as a graph whose

45
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:46,457
edges carry the source's own dates.

46
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:50,653
The footer is measured:

47
00:02:51,093 --> 00:02:53,753
the planner calls and how many were valid first try,

48
00:02:54,033 --> 00:02:57,173
prompt tokens per chunk flat against the full-history estimate,

49
00:02:57,553 --> 00:03:01,183
the median tokens a second, and zero cloud model calls.

50
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:06,633
One data path: Zetaris Lightning is the only route to SEC EDGAR,

51
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:08,393
NOAA and the SIC list,

52
00:03:08,713 --> 00:03:11,433
and the gateway's named templates are the only SQL.

53
00:03:12,253 --> 00:03:15,653
Meterless engines run the chain, the memory and the world model.

54
00:03:16,313 --> 00:03:18,933
Nemotron plans and writes on one local GPU,

55
00:03:18,953 --> 00:03:20,983
and never computes a number.

56
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:28,607
Measured over nine runs: 171 of 171 card claims cited;

57
00:03:28,627 --> 00:03:34,127
join map 6 of 6; 300 of 300 bootstrap resamples;

58
00:03:34,147 --> 00:03:37,567
64 of 76 planner calls valid first try, 1 fallback;

59
00:03:37,587 --> 00:03:40,757
0 memo numbers from the model; 0 cloud calls.

60
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:42,893
Weather-or-Not.

61
00:03:43,113 --> 00:03:46,123
Every number is cited, and every override is signed.
